message: "If you use or build on the Inheritance Test, please cite it as below."
title: "The Inheritance Test — a framework for assessing ownership"
authors:
  - family-names: Gretzinger
    given-names: Julian
version: "1.1"
date-released: 2026-07-12
url: "https://juliangretzinger.com/inheritance-test.html"
repository-code: "https://github.com/juliangretzinger/inheritance-test"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - ownership
  - tokenization
  - tokenised securities
  - structured finance
  - in rem
  - custody
  - settlement
  - RWA
abstract: >-
  An open framework for establishing what the holder of a structured or
  tokenised instrument actually owns. A wrapper inherits the properties of
  its underlying and cannot bestow them; the test runs a structure through
  three gates — economic, legal (in rem), and jurisdictional — to one of
  five verdicts, with a companion operating instruction that lets an AI
  assistant apply the method consistently, returning "indeterminate"
  rather than guessing where the structure cannot be established.
